{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge","id":1452385,"title":"Failure of a rank-challenge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-15T15:37:56-07:00","id":1452385,"title":"Failure of a rank-challenge","content":"So, one has to challenge a higher-ranked Garou in order to rank-up, once one has the requisite Renown. What happens when the challenge fails? Do you lose all that Renown and have to start over from scratch? Do you keep it and challenge the next night? Do you have to wait a moon to challenge again? Lots of rules for ranking up, but as far as I can see, nothing on what happens when your players goof the attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T16:06:51-07:00","id":1452387,"title":"","content":"They don't lose all their Renown, but they probably lose at least a little for screwing up, which means they'd have to re-earn some before they could challenge again. But the game ultimately leaves it up to the character being challenged. If the challenge failed from no fault of the petitioner, there's nothing wrong with letting them re-challenge ASAP. Like say, you're in the middle of a challenge and the Sept comes under attack, causing you to fail? Why not let you start over once the attack is cleaned up?<br /> <br /> The game wants to make the ST and players comfortable with the challenges being hard enough that they can be failed; that means you can't make failing too harsh in the rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T18:28:25-07:00","id":1452400,"title":"","content":"If there are no rules on the matter, I would houserule that you need to wait one full moon cycle before trying again. That fits a werewolf culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T18:43:36-07:00","id":1452403,"title":"","content":"Again though... why force a month as a rule if there's the potential for reasons to allow for retry immediately?<br /> <br /> If the petitioner (a) does so ASAP and those just has the minimum Renown and (b) screws up in a fashion that loses them Renown, the minimum default time is a month anyway: they'd need to earn enough Renown to regain their loss, and have the Rite of Accomplishment performed again, which is traditionally only done at Moots.<br /> <br /> From a &quot;playing the game&quot; perspective, you don't want to force one player that's struggling to get Rank to sit there for months in game time behind the rest of the pack, because you just tossed in a waiting time that's not inherently there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T18:55:00-07:00","id":1452405,"title":"","content":"I don't think there are any written rules to that scenario. That's very common in Werewolf so it leaves a lot for STs to figure out for themselves. Here is what I do.<br /> <br /> 1) There is no Renown loss for simply failing to pass the test. However, if the Garou does something during the test that would normally cause them to lose renown, they of course would lose that.<br /> <br /> 2) The challenge has been failed. They don't get to attempt to try again with that challenge. That is not the same as not being allowed to advance Rank again. It just means they need to challenge a Garou again and start the process over. Depending on what you want done, it might mean they have to challenge the same Garou, or need to challenge a different Garou, or decide whatever they want. There are positives and negatives to both approaches both IC and OOC. You can set any rule you want as the ST for the entire Nation, or have each sept determine any such rules locally.<br /> <br /> 3) The Garou need to wait one lunar month before challenging again. I agree with CajunKhan it fits werewolf culture best. However, this is likely something that is modified by local sept culture. Some septs might require more elaborate preparation to show they are ready again, but I wouldn't make any sept's unique culture to be radically different from everyone else's.<br /> <br /> 4) It is up to the Garou being challenged to determine whether to issue the exact same challenge, a slightly different challenge, or a completely different challenge. It really depends on what they think works best for the circumstances.<br /> <br /> In my setting, the purpose of the Challenge is to demonstrate the Garou is ready for the responsibilities for the next rank within Garou society. Awarding Renown is something that can be politically manipulated, and there are times when a Garou's abilities show he is not ready for the next rank. (Although obviously the challenge itself can also be politically manipulated). When that happens, good Garou being challenged creates a difficult challenge that will cause that Garou to fail in order to teach that Garou they have much more to learn despite having gained the necessary Renown. When the candidate appears to be ready, the challenge tests them enough that they have to demonstrate whatever skill, but should be able to be passed. At least the challenges for Rank 2 (I am ready for adulthood) and Rank 3 (I am an established member of the community and can mentor younger Garou) are usually not too hard to pass. All but the most incompetent Garou should be able to pass those during their lifetime. It isn't until Rank 4 (I am a leader of the Nation) and Rank 5 (I am a hero of the people) that the challenges are so hard that even capable Garou of those levels might fail (or at least take a very long time to achieve). Other STs will handle their challenges differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T23:08:25-07:00","id":1452420,"title":"","content":"Can someone actually explain how &quot;wait a lunar month&quot; is actually in keeping with Garou culture?<br /> <br /> Lunar months are absolutely important sure.<br /> <br /> But challenge culture in Garou society is not governed by lunar months. There's no tradition that says if you challenge the leader of your pack for the top spot, or for a position in the Sept, they're safe for a lunar month no matter what happens. The books present Garou challenge culture as something that happens whenever two Garou need to settle something, so the Garou can all move on after declaring a victor that than having things wait; and possibly emotions fester.<br /> <br /> Where does the idea that &quot;it fits Garou culture,&quot; actually come from if none of their challenge culture revolves around it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T14:05:47-07:00","id":1452532,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms - I think it comes down to the wording that most formal challenges are handled during &quot;The Cracking of The Bone&quot; during Moots. Naturally, you can handle Rank challenges outside of that time, but it does seem natural. I agree wholeheartedly that if the challenge was interrupted so that the petitioner could fulfill their duties to Sept and Gaia, then they should be able to start over ASAP.<br /> <br /> Black Fox - You summed up my take on the process perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T14:47:47-07:00","id":1452542,"title":"","content":"Waiting for the next Moot is going to be waiting either less than or more than a month unless the challenge is issues and failed at the Moot. Considering how many examples challenges aren't something you could do at the Moot, waiting for the next Moot would frequently be less than a month. So... that doesn't really explain, &quot;wait a month,&quot; instead of, &quot;wait for the next moot.&quot;<br /> <br /> As well, while it is tradition for a Sept to have a general Moot once a month, Hearing Moots happen as needed, and Tribal Moots also happen whenever the Tribe wants to meet and deal with their own issues away from the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T07:20:51-07:00","id":1452624,"title":"","content":"I read &quot;wait one lunar month&quot; as synonymous with &quot;wait until the next Sept Moot&quot; since most challenges for Adren and above are unlikely to be completed during a single Moot. To me, it goes something like this:<br /> <br /> * I challenge for Adren at the September Moot.<br /> * I undertake the challenge and fail during the month.<br /> * The Master of the Rite declares the challenge failed (and therefore over) and instructs me to meditate / study / practice / whatever until the next Moot when I can officially challenge again.<br /> * I challenge for Adren at the October Moot.<br /> * ... and hopefully succeed.<br /> <br /> The other types of Moots don't seem appropriate times to handle rank challenges, but your mileage may vary. In the end it should just make internal sense for your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T12:12:31-07:00","id":1452667,"title":"","content":"To me, the main issue is to prevent shotgun challenges where the Challenger fails, and then immediately tries again until he wins. In that scenario losing the original challenge would almost be meaningless. So there should be a reasonable period of time before the person challenges for the same issue again. So what's a reasonable amount of time? Well, a lunar cycle makes sense for Werewolf.<br /> <br /> There are certainly other time periods an ST could choose instead, but I think a lunar cycle works best since its reasonable, not too long, and thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> Now when it comes to other kinds of challenges (those not about advancing rank), a lunar month may not necessarily be appropriate. There could be justification for an even earlier re-challenge, or lack of justification that would push the next opportunity way later than one month or even permanently denied. In those cases (challenge for pack or sept leadership, resolving bad blood between two Garou, rival claimants for territory, etc.) there's probably a variety of factors that need to be considered before a re-challenge could be permitted. After all, the purpose of a challenge is to decide the issue so Garou can move on. Allowing someone to constantly bring up the same issue again and again negates that. <br /> <br /> Now the Garou likely have a long series of precedents that establishes such times in their law code, the Litany or just tradition in general. So within the setting most Garou, and certainly their Philodoxes, likely know what's appropriate in most situations. But these are not things most games need, and neither STs or Players want to slog through an actual legal code (no matter how short - and remember that in its full form it takes hours to recite the entire Litany, and every tribe and sept has a slightly different version) to determine these things so it comes down to an ST's decision on the spot so the game can move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T16:31:08-07:00","id":1452711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452667#post1452667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the main issue is to prevent shotgun challenges where the Challenger fails, and then immediately tries again until he wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does this need to be policed by any rules, either game rules or in-universe rules? The rules already say that (a) the challenged Garou doesn't have to accept and (b) they can make the challenge whatever they want.<br /> <br /> If the higher ranked Garou think you're being an idiot because you're trying something like this, they hit you with a challenge that could take months to do, and be nearly impossible to manage successfully. There's no reason to let this work unless the higher Ranks want to let it work. Getting yourself a reputation for this in a fashion that annoys your superiors isn't going to go well without some minimum waiting period.<br /> <br /> When none of the higher Ranks will even hear your challenge, and the Master of the Challenge backs them up if you try to use it to force the matter at a Moot, you've screwed yourself far harder than any time limit is going to do.<br /> <br /> There's no support for the idea that you can just keep challenging over and over until it works, and nothing but a minimum wait period can stop you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, a lunar cycle makes sense for Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>Why? You're not just affirming ThomasM here.<br /> <br /> If you botch learning a Rite, you have to wait three lunar months before you can try again, and learning intervals are based on weeks x Rite level.<br /> <br /> Why shouldn't the wait period be a number of weeks equal to Rank, but three months if you mess up the challenge really badly then? What makes a flat month &quot;make sense&quot; for the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T18:14:17-07:00","id":1452724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452711#post1452711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does this need to be policed by any rules, either game rules or in-universe rules? The rules already say that (a) the challenged Garou doesn't have to accept and (b) they can make the challenge whatever they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the characters who decide they don't want to accept a challenge typically have a reason for doing so. It makes sense that in many situations there is some kind of standard or guidelines within the customs of the Nation. There shouldn't be any issue with an ST deciding that any rule of this kind is a custom of the Garou or the sept in these cases. I like to have some kind of standard in my game so it helps me lead to consistent rulings. And if I diverge from that for whatever reason (one tribe is more lax, this sept has a different kind of totem, this case is not like all the other cases), then I can still evaluate that against a standard. It helps me as an ST run the game, and it helps the PCs in their own roleplay when they know &quot;this is how this is done.&quot; If such an approach doesn't work for you, fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452711#post1452711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no support for the idea that you can just keep challenging over and over until it works, and nothing but a minimum wait period can stop you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if there was any support on this issue, the OP wouldn't have started the thread. All we can do is say what we would do and explain our reasons. Putting down a Garou custom for your game that would address a concern you have about the setting doesn't mean &quot;nothing but that can stop you.&quot; Those are your words, not mine. I never said &quot;nothing but this can stop that.&quot; You purposefully try to create a weak version of a person's opinions so you can attack a straw man. I explained that I didn't like the potential for shotgun challenges. Your response to that is Garou could just say no. But it doesn't explain why they would do so. Or why other Garou would act the same. Presumably they just would for no reason. But if someone decides this is the custom of the Garou in my games, then it provides a standard for all Garou as opposed to their personal whims.<br /> <br /> Why does it offend you so much that someone decides to put in a time limit based on the lunar cycle? Simply because that's not how you run in your games? That's fine, and you can give reasons why you prefer a different approach. That can lead to a fruitful discussion as people can determine on their own what approach has the most merit for their own chronicles. But that means discussing in good faith. Not recharacterizing someone's words into a weaker version so it's easier for you to attack it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452711#post1452711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? You're not just affirming ThomasM here.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what? ThomasM has his own opinions and can defend them. Simply because you don't like his interpretation either doesn't mean all of us are using the same standard or have to defend each other's opinions just because they are generally similar.<br /> <br /> If you want to make an argument on behalf of three months, or number of weeks equal to Rank, or any other alternate standard, go ahead. Make those arguments yourself. Explain how you think it works better than a lunar cycle. So far, if you have a better standard, you haven't shared it.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms, you have a very bad habit of becoming belligerent in your arguments whenever someone's opinions or tastes regarding an area of the game is vaguely defined is different from yours. Your tone frequently becomes more and more hostile, and there's never any excuse for it. I hope you refrain from it in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T19:14:40-07:00","id":1452726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452724#post1452724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If such an approach doesn't work for you, fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's just an out-of-character thing for managing the game, why do you keep trying to claim it &quot;makes sense,&quot; in-universe and yet refuse to actually explain why it makes sense?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never said &quot;nothing but this can stop that.&quot; </div> </div> </div>You said, &quot;...and then immediately tries again until he wins.&quot;<br /> <br /> I fail to see how my rephrasing is meaningfully different or leads to a strawman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You purposefully try to create a weak version of a person's opinions so you can attack a straw man. </div> </div> </div>Justify this claim or retract it please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it doesn't explain why they would do so. </div> </div> </div>Did you read the part where I did? Because I did.<br /> <br /> Don't accuse me of making a strawman argument when you're literally lying about the content of my posts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why does it offend you so much that someone decides to put in a time limit based on the lunar cycle? </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it &quot;offended&quot; my. So you know, there's you lying about my posts again.<br /> <br /> I asked for you to actually justify the statement you made. Why is it so offensive to you that you might be asked to do so?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's fine, and you can give reasons why you prefer a different approach </div> </div> </div>I did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That can lead to a fruitful discussion as people can determine on their own what approach has the most merit for their own chronicles. </div> </div> </div>How can we have a discussion if you're not going to answer a simple question?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that means discussing in good faith. </div> </div> </div>Pot. Kettle. Black. Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So what? </div> </div> </div>ThomasM actually attempted to answer my question, you continue to dodge it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So far, if you have a better standard, you haven't shared it. </div> </div> </div>Actually, I did. My standard is the book's standard: whatever the NPCs feel is appropriate. I want Garou to actually engage in politics, means the &quot;whims&quot; of their superiors actually have to be a thing, not some arbitrary rule that says this is how it works for everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heavy Arms, you have a very bad habit of becoming belligerent in your arguments whenever someone's opinions or tastes regarding an area of the game is vaguely defined is different from yours. Your tone frequently becomes more and more hostile, and there's never any excuse for it. I hope you refrain from it in this thread. </div> </div> </div>Black Fox, you have a very bad habit of ad hominem attacks on anyone that disagrees with you instead of engaging in good faith with them. Your tone frequently drips with condescension, arrogance, and aggressive attempts to chase dissenters from the forums. There's no excuse for it. I've lost hope you'll refrain from such in any thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T00:05:11-07:00","id":1452868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's just an out-of-character thing for managing the game, why do you keep trying to claim it &quot;makes sense,&quot; In-universe and yet refuse to actually explain why it makes sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's used for both OOC and IC reasons. OOC for me as ST in order to better run the NPCs IC. Obviously the behavior of NPCs in an in-universe thing. And it directly impacts the PCs in-universe whether it is them making a challenge or them dealing with an NPC going to them for a challenge. I thought that was quite clear in the post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said, &quot;...and then immediately tries again until he wins.&quot;<br /> <br /> I fail to see how my rephrasing is meaningfully different or leads to a strawman.</div> </div> </div> </div>At no point did I say that was the ONLY way to prevent shotgun challenges. Yet your response was \u201cThere's no support for the idea that you can just keep challenging over and over until it works, and <i>nothing but a minimum wait period</i> can stop you.\u201d (my emphasis)<br /> <br /> You choose to mischaracterize my statement as some kind of absolute because you know an absolute statement is easier to disprove. This was done to a post where I even mention that there can be a variety of mitigating factors that influence things. Yet you insist on treating it as an absolute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Justify this claim or retract it please.</div> </div> </div> </div>See above. This was all explained in the original post.<br /> <br /> But that isn't the only time on this thread. Earlier you stated \u201c force one player that's struggling to get Rank to sit there for months in game time\u201d. Where did this \u201cmonths\u201d in game time occur when everyone is talking about at most one lunar month? But I guess complaining about \u201cmonths\u201d sound better, even though that may only take minutes in real time for that game time to pass.<br /> <br /> It's not that you don't have a relevant point, but that you choose to mischaracterize what people are saying so that you can attack a weaker argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you read the part where I did? Because I did.<br /> <br /> Don't accuse me of making a strawman argument when you're literally lying about the content of my posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>After a second reading of your posts I still don't see it. Where do you explain why a Garou would decline a challenge made immediately after failing one? The only thing that comes close is when you explain the Garou being challenge has the right to decline, or that they could make the challenge so hard it would dissuade them. Simply having the right to decline doesn't explain why they would decline. Unless that Garou already has an idea of what a reasonable amount of time is before the next challenge, he doesn't have a reason to decline or come up with a punishing challenge.<br /> <br /> Presumably you have your own reasons why a Garou would decline, but you didn't articulate them. If I just happened to miss it, you can direct me to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say it &quot;offended&quot; my. So you know, there's you lying about my posts again.<br /> <br /> I asked for you to actually justify the statement you made. Why is it so offensive to you that you might be asked to do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you didn't say that specifically. But one doesn't need to say they were offended to act like that. It's certainly what I am perceiving. I see it in many of your posts when you come across someone's personal opinion in the game that you disagree with. You increasingly become belligerent in your posts when they don't back down. And it's not just me. I've read other threads (including ones I've never posted on) when this situation occurs, and other forum members have mentioned the same thing. And usually your response is to escalate even further. I don't know if the others on this thread have the same interpretation I do, but it's certainly what I am seeing.<br /> <br /> Several people on this thread have stated they like the idea of waiting a lunar month for a failed challenge. Despite mentioning in your very next post that you understand that lunar month cycles are important to Garou culture, you continue to ask people why they want to use that standard. Then when they answer in more detail, you basically say it isn't good enough and demand they provide even more justification. Except that in your specific words you claim they aren't answering you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did.</div> </div> </div> </div>You gave a bizarre scenario where a challenge is issued, the caern is attacked during it, and that causes the challenge to automatically fail, and therefore the just thing to do is allow the Garou to immediately rechallenge.<br /> <br /> But why would the caern being attacked cause the challenge to fail? At worst, wouldn't it just be a case of the challenge being interrupted and it just would resume after the crisis was over? I actually don't see this as an issue, or something an ST would actually do in game. It seems like a very contrived scenario just in order for you to say your opinion is superior. I'm sure we can all come up with a strictly worded challenge that would cause a Garou to fail through no fault of their own, but I don't think that is typical nor the scenario of the original thread poster.<br /> <br /> At best, it's just an argument for \u201cthere should be exceptions for mitigating circumstances.\u201d That doesn't actually invalidate the other poster's opinions. And I think that is why you mischaracterized statements as being absolute even though no one has said that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can we have a discussion if you're not going to answer a simple question?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been answered multiple times. You've just chosen to ignore them.<br /> <br /> An association of the lunar month with Garou culture is self-evident, as you yourself admitted in your third post. Then I explained I thought such a rule would be helpful to prevent shotgun challenges, and that the time delay seemed reasonable, not over long, and thematically appropriate. How does this not answer your question?<br /> <br /> It's obvious you don't like that answer, but it doesn't mean it hasn't been given. Continuing to ask other forum members to keep providing responses gets close to harassment in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pot. Kettle. Black. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've been answering your replies in much more good faith than you have. But it's true when you wrestle with a pig, you're going to get mud on yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ThomasM actually attempted to answer my question, you continue to dodge it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I haven't. I've answered it and even given my reasons why I like it OOC and IC. You just don't like them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I did. My standard is the book's standard: whatever the NPCs feel is appropriate. I want Garou to actually engage in politics, means the &quot;whims&quot; of their superiors actually have to be a thing, not some arbitrary rule that says this is how it works for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the personal whims of NPCs isn't a very helpful standard. First, it does nothing to help the OP figure out what to do in his chronicle. There are times being told \u201cwhatever you want\u201d is what an ST needs to hear so they feel empowered to make their own decision. But when someone is looking for guidance, it doesn't help. Second, I don't think IC that whatever an NPC feels appropriate is the correct answer. There is a big difference on an informed value judgment based on some sort of Garou custom or tradition that provides an appropriate scope or guidance, that can be adjusted as needed, and something merely based on whim.<br /> <br /> If it only some \u201cwhim\u201d with nothing behind it, then there is too much risk that whim can be completely inappropriate. The challenged Garou may have the right to make a challenge as easy or hard as they want, but in-universe there is likely guidelines that the Garou know are appropriate. And if their personal whim goes outside that, that Garou will likely be taken aside by the others and have it explained to them that they acted inappropriately. There's a reason we are given examples of the kind of challenges appropriate at each Rank.<br /> <br /> I don't think Philodoxes or any other judges simply do whatever they want. Their decisions should be informed by Garou culture (whether national, tribal, or by sept). The books provide some guidance in this regard, but not for every situation. So STs need to come up with standards on their own, or sometimes like the OP reach out to other players and see what they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452726#post1452726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Fox, you have a very bad habit of ad hominem attacks on anyone that disagrees with you instead of engaging in good faith with them. Your tone frequently drips with condescension, arrogance, and aggressive attempts to chase dissenters from the forums. There's no excuse for it. I've lost hope you'll refrain from such in any thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are holding up a mirror here.<br /> <br /> I will leave it to the other forum members to decide which of us, if any or both, fall into our assessments of the other.<br /> <br /> If you or any other forum member thinks any of my posts have been against forum rules or internet courtesy in general, they can report me to the mods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T04:11:30-07:00","id":1452881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452868#post1452868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At no point did I say that was the ONLY way to prevent shotgun challenges.</div> </div> </div> </div>You stated it was necessary to prevent it. You said &quot;there should be a reasonable period of time,&quot; and without such a thing failing the original challenge is meaningless.<br /> <br /> You do realize that part of good faith discussion is &quot;charitable reading&quot; where you don't read as much negativity as you can stand muster into other people's posts? That you should consider you really might have phrased your point in a way where my reading is valid, and not immediately jump to claiming bad faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You choose to mischaracterize my statement as some kind of absolute because you know an absolute statement is easier to disprove. </div> </div> </div>You stated your opinion as an absolute. There should be a waiting time. You've continually defended that and even attacked the idea of situations where it would be reasonable to skip a waiting time as, &quot;bizziare.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This was done to a post where I even mention that there can be a variety of mitigating factors that influence things. </div> </div> </div>You presented no mitigating factors to this specific claim. You said it could be a bit flexible by local Sept culture. That is the only variation on waiting period you offered in your post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See above. This was all explained in the original post. </div> </div> </div>You stated as a matter of fact, that I purposefully did something. You have provided no evidence of intent. Just ad hominem bad faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where did this \u201cmonths\u201d in game time occur when everyone is talking about at most one lunar month? </div> </div> </div>What, exactly, do you think happens if you fail more than once if the minimum time between challenges is a month? Months go by. That's the direct logic of the rule you've created. If a character is struggling with their Rank challenges and has to do it multiple times, it starts to stretch out over months.<br /> <br /> That's not a strawman, that's pointing out the implications of the house rule. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I guess complaining about \u201cmonths\u201d sound better, even though that may only take minutes in real time for that game time to pass. </div> </div> </div>I guess ad hominem arguments are better for you than good faith ones?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where do you explain why a Garou would decline a challenge made immediately after failing one? </div> </div> </div>&quot;If the higher ranked Garou <b>think you're being an idiot</b> because you're trying something like this, they hit you with a challenge that could take months to do, and be nearly impossible to manage successfully. There's no reason to let this work unless the higher Ranks want to let it work. Getting yourself a reputation for this in a fashion that <b>annoys your superiors</b> isn't going to go well without some minimum waiting period.<br /> <br /> When none of the higher Ranks will even hear your challenge, and the Master of the Challenge backs them up if you try to use it to force the matter at a Moot, you've screwed yourself far harder than any time limit is going to do.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simply having the right to decline doesn't explain why they would decline. </div> </div> </div>So, are those bold parts not statements of &quot;why?&quot; or did you just not read that part?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless that Garou already has an idea of what a reasonable amount of time is before the next challenge, he doesn't have a reason to decline or come up with a punishing challenge. </div> </div> </div>Sure they do. You don't need a societal standard to come up with a subjective opinion on something like this.<br /> <br /> Is there some rulebook somewhere that says how long a parent should ground their child after they stay out too late for the third time? Or is that simple something a parent figures out based on their own experiences?<br /> <br /> All that's necessary is the next Garou the petitioner challenges to think it's a bad idea to challenge right away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But one doesn't need to say they were offended to act like that. </div> </div> </div>It's text, you can't see how I'm acting. You're reading offense into it. Do you not, in the slightest, see how hypocritical it is for you to berate me for mischaractizing things, while you're essentially admitting that you chose to interpret this negatively in order to justify calling my posts bad?<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm just annoyed because you're not answering a question that seems pretty simple, but I keep having to ask it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see it in many of your posts when you come across someone's personal opinion in the game that you disagree with. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's called &quot;confirmation bias.&quot; People decide I'm a bad guy, so they bias their reading of what I say worse, and worse, so to further confirm that I'm the bad one. Then the echo chamber with each other, and so on, and me calling them out on it is just me being &quot;belligerent,&quot; instead of them actually having to think that maybe they're part of the problem!<br /> <br /> But please, go on about how horrible I am in a fashion that only continues to reinforce that most of it is just people reading into things that aren't there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then when they answer in more detail, you basically say it isn't good enough and demand they provide even more justification. Except that in your specific words you claim they aren't answering you. </div> </div> </div>Nobody's actually answered in more detail. ThomasM changed the standard from &quot;month&quot; to &quot;until the next Moot.&quot; You have yet to make any statement other than, &quot;it makes sense.&quot; I provided other waiting periods that are important to Garou culture as evidence that a month isn't the only option, and instead of trying to explain why a month is more sensible than that standard, you just deflect with, &quot;well you can run it that way if you want,&quot; and thus, you have never actually answer the question. Just repeating that it makes sense, or it's appropriate, or its thematic, doesn't explain why of the many periods of time that are important to Garou culture it's the one that's the culturally best fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But why would the caern being attacked cause the challenge to fail? </div> </div> </div>This literally happened to one of my characters: His challenge was to best one of the other PCs in a contest,and that PC died in the fight to defend the Caern, so it was impossible to fulfill the challenge and ruled as having failed.<br /> <br /> Another one of my character almost lost a challenge to craft a Fetish within a period of time, because a bad series of tactical choices and rolls led to the building on the Bawn where his work was stored going up in flames and he had to run in to rescue all his work/materials/chiminage so he wouldn't have to start over and probably wouldn't have had time to do so.<br /> <br /> I can come up with dozens of similar scenarios, none of which are out of place in the game (though playstyle might impact how likely they are).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems like a very contrived scenario just in order for you to say your opinion is superior. </div> </div> </div>See, there you go again, just flat out admitting that you're choosing to read in bad faith. Again, do you not see the hypocrisy here? You're going on about picking out the tiniest wording to claim I'm purposefully trying to twist the whole thread in my favor, but you just dismiss things I say as bizarre and contrived; not with any actual reasoning for those labels, but as a flat ad hominem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's been answered multiple times. You've just chosen to ignore them. </div> </div> </div>Where have you answered it besides some different rephrasing of, &quot;it just makes sense?&quot; And not &quot;oh and I like it OOC for structure for my games,&quot; because that's not answering the actual question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does this not answer your question? </div> </div> </div>Because the question is how is it thematically appropriate, instead of just an arbitrary pick of one period of time important to Garou culture. &quot;It's thematically appropriate,&quot; is just, &quot;well it makes sense,&quot; in different words. So it doesn't answer why it makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's obvious you don't like that answer, but it doesn't mean it hasn't been given. </div> </div> </div>I don't like that <u>response</u> because it's not an answer to the question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Continuing to ask other forum members to keep providing responses gets close to harassment in my opinion. </div> </div> </div>Oh yay, more ad hominem barbs!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I've been answering your replies in much more good faith than you have. </div> </div> </div>Of course you do. Do you think I don't see it in the opposite fashion or something?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it's true when you wrestle with a pig, you're going to get mud on yourself. </div> </div> </div>So, back to that whole confirmation bias thing? If I called you a pig, would you be sitting there like, &quot;well, OK, that's kinda fair, I've been a bit underhanded about this,&quot; or would you be mashing the report button ASAP, and the PMing people that don't like me to do the same, and hope the mods smack me down for a personal attack (you know, because I'm the belligerent one regardless of who said what)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, it does nothing to help the OP figure out what to do in his chronicle. </div> </div> </div>The OP never asked for help for their chronicle. They asked what the rules actually are. You're assuming that the OP wants house rules on what to do, despite no request for them. So dragging the OP into this doesn't pan out for your argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, I don't think IC that whatever an NPC feels appropriate is the correct answer. </div> </div> </div>It's the answer in the books... you can't really argue that it's &quot;incorrect&quot; objectively even if you don't like how it plays out for your games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The challenged Garou may have the right to make a challenge as easy or hard as they want, but in-universe there is likely guidelines that the Garou know are appropriate. </div> </div> </div>Sure, their own personal experiences gaining rank in the first place, and seeing others do it. If you want to house rule in more, that's your prerogative, but don't pretend that's not what you're doing. Nowhere in the books is it stated that the challenged Garou would get pulled aside for answering challenges &quot;wrong,&quot; because there's no universal standard in the books for them to be wrong against.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a reason we are given examples of the kind of challenges appropriate at each Rank. </div> </div> </div>So... the ST and players have a starting point on what to do? Like the book says?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T13:30:51-07:00","id":1452984,"title":"","content":"Like always it becomes pointless to discuss anything with you. Your accuse others of the very bad behaviors you display yourself whenever you are called out. And in the end you fall back on the tactic of acting like someone's quick forum post is the equivalent of a doctoral dissertation with extended footnotes, and if they haven't, that means you're &quot;right&quot; because you always claim something that wasn't mentioned is proof of whatever you want to accuse them of. Despite never using the words &quot;only&quot;, &quot;always&quot;, or &quot;never,&quot; you insist I must have meant an absolute statement. Why? Because that's the only way you can &quot;win&quot; the argument. And this despite your own insistence people adopt a &quot;charitable reading&quot;!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452881#post1452881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's called &quot;confirmation bias.&quot; People decide I'm a bad guy, so they bias their reading of what I say worse, and worse, so to further confirm that I'm the bad one. Then the echo chamber with each other, and so on, and me calling them out on it is just me being &quot;belligerent,&quot; instead of them actually having to think that maybe they're part of the problem!</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you should start asking yourself if there's a reason people are telling you this instead of sneaking back into the comfort that it must be everyone else who is the problem and your own behavior is impeachable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T19:50:59-07:00","id":1453007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1452385-failure-of-a-rank-challenge?p=1452984#post1452984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like always it becomes pointless to discuss anything with you. Your accuse others of the very bad behaviors you display yourself whenever you are called out. And in the end you fall back on the tactic of acting like someone's quick forum post is the equivalent of a doctoral dissertation with extended footnotes, and if they haven't, that means you're &quot;right&quot; because you always claim something that wasn't mentioned is proof of whatever you want to accuse them of. Despite never using the words &quot;only&quot;, &quot;always&quot;, or &quot;never,&quot; you insist I must have meant an absolute statement. Why? Because that's the only way you can &quot;win&quot; the argument. And this despite your own insistence people adopt a &quot;charitable reading&quot;!<br /> <br /> Maybe you should start asking yourself if there's a reason people are telling you this instead of sneaking back into the comfort that it must be everyone else who is the problem and your own behavior is impeachable.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>If you have a problem with the posters, report them. Instead, you have engaged in personal attack. Take an infraction and leave the thread.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T04:00:26-07:00","id":1453342,"title":"","content":"In my opinion it depends on the challenge and the petitioner in question, as well as the date.<br /> <br /> In most cases challenges for rank should be public, the &quot;breaking of the bone&quot; is the appropriate phase of a Moot to do so and it happens monthly.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, there might be challenges that take a long time to accomplish. &quot;Building a fetish&quot; to increase rank doesn't pair well with &quot;Children of Gaia tend to carry parts of a would-be fetish over their heart for a year&quot;. So, depending on what parts of garou culture hidden somewhere in the multitude of books by various authors the ST/players are aware of an see as appropriate for their chronicle/home sept the challenges my vary.<br /> If such a challenge fails, it should also be made public. This might be at a moot, but possibly the sept is gathered for a seasonal rite or some other event and it is made public there. Same goes for issuing the challenge. If it is reasonably public, so people could interfere if they wanted to (similar to a Rite of Accomplishment, of which I think is made use to bestow the rank formally) it is fine.<br /> <br /> Petitioner and the Challenged should take time to revisit what lead to failing the challenge and address that in a new challenge. So, sometime taking time simply makes sense.<br /> With that in mind, someone could always challenge, but the challenged garou might not have a suitable task to perform right away. So, this can also be an acceptable reason to take some time, like &quot;I challenge you now, since it is a public event and I want my claim to be known. I'm fully aware that you consider the tasks you issue carefully and accept to wait until you can issue a task worthy of someone in the status I claim&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}